1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:03,020
The Wurtz reaction joins two molecules.

2
00:00:03,020 --> 00:00:13,111
Two bromoethane molecules with sodium in dry ether: the sodium takes both bromines, and the two ethyl groups bond together, giving butane.

3
00:00:13,111 --> 00:00:20,377
It doubles the carbon chain, so from a single halide it can only make alkanes with an even number of carbons.

4
00:00:20,377 --> 00:00:25,065
Mixing two halides gives a messy mixture of three alkanes.

